-# The button that replaces the control characters a validation just named. No
-# local gate: this renders only where the caller has already established there is
-# something to replace.
-#
-# `form:` rather than nesting, because the two places the offer belongs are both
-# outside #raw_xml_form — the refusal banner above it, and the Turbo-replaced
-# preview pane beside it. A submitter outside a form still fires that form's
-# submit event, so the editor controller still syncs the Ace buffer into the
-# hidden field, and the curator's unsaved edits are what gets repaired.
-#
-# It must stay a Turbo submission. Per-form CSRF tokens bind the form's token to
-# the form's own action, so a `formaction` override can only authenticate on the
-# global token Turbo sends in the X-CSRF-Token header — opting out of Turbo here
-# earns a 422 from InvalidAuthenticityToken. Save relies on the same thing.
%button.btn.btn-outline-danger.btn-sm.mt-2{type: "submit", form: "raw_xml_form", formaction: xml_repair_path}
  %i.fas.fa-screwdriver-wrench.me-1
  Replace the control characters
